! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260's I60S1 -- "SUBROUTINE TO CLR INDS
! 0-19, AND CHK THAT THEY ARE CLRD."  PDF pp.83-84 (printed pp.80-81),
! octal 022741.00-023021.00, transcribed VERBATIM at the listing's own
! addresses and checked bit-exactly by verify_ax5b_160s1_listing.py.
!
! THIS FILE IS THE HEAD ONLY, 022741.00-023021.00 (PDF pp.83-84).  The
! TAIL, 023021.40-023041.00 on p.85, is programs/ax5b_160s1_tail.strap
! -- and it holds the row that matters most in the whole subroutine:
! the RETURN, "I60SX1 $BD,0" at 023041.00.  I60S1 returns via a BRANCH
! DISABLED, so every block that calls "SIC,I60SX1 / B,I60S1" runs
! DISABLED afterwards unless it enables for itself.  That fact settled
! an open question about routine 1262's TEST 3A/3B; see
! programs/ax5b_162_test3b.strap.  Read the two files together.

! THIS IS THE ROUTINE docs/NEXT.md MYTHOLOGISED.  The file opened with
! "Prerequisite: SSIP's I60S1/I60SX1 save/restore harness, reported at
! ax5b pp.41-44.  Nothing from 1260 can run without it."  Every clause
! of that was wrong:
!   * it is not SSIP's -- it is local to routine 1260;
!   * it is not a save/restore harness -- it CLEARS INDICATORS 0-19
!     and checks each went off;
!   * it is not at pp.41-44 -- it is at pp.83-84, 022741.00;
!   * and four blocks of 1260 were transcribed without it before
!     anyone opened the page.
! What it IS actually needed for is the p.71 COMPARISON driver
! (ax5b_160105_compare.strap), which calls it.
!
! THE SHAPE, repeated once per indicator: branch-on-indicator-and-zero
! to skip if already clear, then TI,1,11.0,$X1 -- TRANSMIT IMMEDIATE
! one word FROM word 11, the indicator register, INTO $X1 -- then KVI
! against that indicator's mask and a branch to SERS naming it:
! "-UNABLE TO CLEAR MK.", "-UNABLE TO CLR IK OR ABOVE IND.", then IJ,
! EK, TS, CPUS, EKJ, UNRJ, CBJ, EPGK, UK, EE, EOP, CS, and finally
! "IND NO. 14".
!
! FIFTEEN USES OF TRANSMIT IMMEDIATE, all identical
! ("13.00 80 000021.02 A0"), each a FULL WORD at an ODD half-word.
! Before TRANSMIT_CODES landed this routine could not have been
! assembled at all.
!
! AND IT FOUND AN ASSEMBLER BUG.  Its one XW row --
! "XW,$+1.07,(8)300000,(8)014000,4" at 023016.00 -- was the single
! mismatch in 45 rows: expected flag byte 46, produced 06.  XW's
! FOURTH OPERAND IS THREE BITS, IBM 25-27 (the index flag plus the two
! spare bits), and strap_asm.py masked it to one.  p.114's own BIT
! table settles it in three adjacent rows: BIT25 is "XW,0,0,0,4",
! BIT26 is ",2", BIT27 is ",1", printing bits 25, 26 and 27
! respectively.  Fixed; see strap_asm.py's XW arm.
!
! ENCODING ONLY.  Running it needs I60DMP (023301.00) and the SERS
! error routine, neither transcribed -- and the point of having it is
! the p.71 block, which needs more besides.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: none, where this header used to say "one.  Numeric
! labels prefixed L (160S1, 160DMP)."  The prefix was there because
! this assembler reads a leading digit as an address; the leading
! glyph was measured at 600 dpi and it is the LETTER I, so the deck's
! I60S1 and I60DMP are legal STRAP-1 symbols as printed and are
! written unaltered (docs/listing_typography.md -- I60S1 at ax5b
! p.83 is one of the rows that carries the measurement, "I 12, 6 45,
! 0 48, S 48, 1 34").  Every external is given by SYN at the address
! this block's own rows print for it.

I60DMP SYN, (8)23301.0
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0
        SLC, (8)22741.0
I60S1  SX,  $X1, I60DMP        ! -SUBROUTINE TO CLR INDS 0-19,
        BMKZ, $+.32              ! -AND CHK THAT THEY ARE CLRD.
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)400000.0
        BXL, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS
        BIKZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)200000.0
        BXL, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS
        BIJZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)100000.0
        BXL, $+1.32
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS
        BEKZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)40000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        LVI, $X1, (8)777777.40
        SV,  $X1, 1.0
        BTSZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)20000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        B,   $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)10000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BEKJZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)4000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BUNRJZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)2000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BCBJZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)1000.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BEPGKZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)400.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BUKZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)200.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BEEZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)100.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BEOPZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)40.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        BCSZ, $+.32
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)20.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        CNOP
        XW,  $+1.07, (8)300000, (8)014000, 4
        TI,  1, 11.0, $X1
        KVI, $X1, (8)10.0
        SIC, SEN
        BZXL, SERS
        END, I60S1
